=== the condition of an -If combinator is named as such
--- SELECT sumIf(a) FROM l
Code: 43. Illegal type UInt32 of the last argument of an aggregate function with the If suffix: the last argument is the condition and must be UInt8. If the condition is missing, it goes after the arguments of the aggregate function. (ILLEGAL_TYPE_OF_ARGUMENT)
--- SELECT sumIf(a, t) FROM l
Code: 43. Illegal type UInt32 of the last argument of an aggregate function with the If suffix: the last argument is the condition and must be UInt8. If the condition is missing, it goes after the arguments of the aggregate function. (ILLEGAL_TYPE_OF_ARGUMENT)
--- SELECT avgIf(a) FROM l
Code: 43. Illegal type UInt32 of the last argument of an aggregate function with the If suffix: the last argument is the condition and must be UInt8. If the condition is missing, it goes after the arguments of the aggregate function. (ILLEGAL_TYPE_OF_ARGUMENT)
--- SELECT countIf(a) FROM l
Code: 43. Illegal type UInt32 of the last argument of an aggregate function with the If suffix: the last argument is the condition and must be UInt8. If the condition is missing, it goes after the arguments of the aggregate function. (ILLEGAL_TYPE_OF_ARGUMENT)

=== an ASOF join says that the inequality is needed in addition to the equalities
--- SELECT * FROM l ASOF JOIN r ON l.a = r.a
Code: 403. ASOF join requires one inequality predicate (<, <=, > or >=) in the JOIN ON expression, in addition to the equality predicates. (INVALID_JOIN_ON_EXPRESSION)

